## Database Tables
- `companies` — tenants (slug = subdomain)
- `visitors` — global, deduplicated by phone number
- `checkins` — per-visit records with photo, host, status
- `materials` — in/out tracking with return flag

## API Endpoints (backend port 4000)
```
POST /api/checkin          Create check-in
PATCH /api/checkin/:id/out Check-out visitor
GET  /api/checkin/today    Today's list
GET  /api/visitor          List visitors
GET  /api/visitor/search   Search by name/phone
POST /api/material         Log material
GET  /api/material/active  Pending returns
GET  /api/stats/summary    Dashboard numbers
```

## Next.js API Routes (frontend port 3000)
```
POST /api/otp/send         Detect returning visitor + send OTP
POST /api/otp/verify       Verify OTP from Redis
POST /api/checkin          Final check-in submit
POST /api/upload/photo     Webcam photo → Cloudinary/Storage
POST /api/material/log     Log material entry
```

## Multi-tenant Flow
1. User hits `techcorp.visbot.in`
2. `middleware.ts` extracts slug `techcorp`
3. Sets `x-company-slug` header
4. Supabase RLS filters all data by `company_id`
5. Each company sees only their visitors/check-ins

## Deployment
- **Vercel**: push `frontend/` — auto deploys on git push
- **Railway**: push `backend/` — uses `railway.json` config
- **Supabase**: run `npx supabase db push` after schema changes
